#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-CG0093 expect=noViolation domain=PP
# Rule:Description: Raise an error when --ELTM, --TPTNUM, --TPT, --STINT, and --ENINT are not present in the dataset but --TPTREF is present.
#note "D23 direction 1 -- the false positive this edit removes. PP is the one SDTMIG 3.4 domain that carries --STINT/--ENINT, and it carries NONE of --ELTM/--TPTNUM/--TPT (which exist in 25 other domains but not PP). PPTPTREF is present. Before the edit all three sheet conjuncts were satisfied by absence and the rule fired on every PP record, even though PP does anchor its timing -- just not with the three variables the sheet names. Neuter by deleting the --STINT and --ENINT conjuncts from CDISC-CG0093.yaml: this scenario then reports 2 violations and goes red."
dataset PP label="Pharmacokinetics Parameters"
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN   type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID  type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col PPSEQ    type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col PPTESTCD type=Char label="Parameter Short Name"
col PPSTRESN type=Num  label="Numeric Result/Finding in Std Units"
col PPSTINT  type=Char label="Start of Assessment Interval"
col PPENINT  type=Char label="End of Assessment Interval"
col PPTPTREF type=Char label="Time Point Reference"
---
CDISCPILOT01 | PP | 01-701-1015 | 1 | AUCALL | 123.4 | P0D | P1D | DOSING
CDISCPILOT01 | PP | 01-701-1015 | 2 | CMAX   |  45.6 | P0D | P1D | DOSING
---
